@* The chrome every top-level screen shares: the bar across the top, the dialog its Feedback
   button opens, and the centred column the page's own content sits in.

   A component the pages wrap themselves in, rather than markup in MainLayout, because the bar
   belongs on the welcome and workload screens and NOT on /install/{id}, /updates, /licenses or
   /debug -- hosting it in the layout would mean the layout inspecting the current route to decide.

   It exists at all because the three moving parts were hand-assembled per page: a third screen
   that added <TopBar> and forgot <FeedbackDialog> would get a Feedback button that silently did
   nothing, and no test would have caught it. *@

<div class="screen">
    <TopBar OnFeedback="() => _feedbackOpen = true" />

    <div class="screen-body">
        @ChildContent
    </div>

    <FeedbackDialog Visible="_feedbackOpen" OnClose="() => _feedbackOpen = false" />
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    private bool _feedbackOpen;
}
